{
  "_comment": [
    "Declared return types of library methods, so a call chained on a library",
    "call (em.createQuery(q).executeUpdate()) knows the type it is called on.",
    "Per language, then per qualified type, then '<method>/<argument count>'",
    "('<method>/*' for varargs) to the qualified return type. Only documented",
    "API signatures belong here. A method whose return type is a type",
    "parameter (TypedQuery<X>.getSingleResult(), Map<K,V>.get()) is left out:",
    "its static type is not known, so the chain stops and stays a gap. A",
    "primitive or void return ends the chain.",
    "A raw generic type (Stream for Stream<R>) is a known receiver type even when its type argument is not."
  ],
